              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Line' />
            <encodings>
              <color column='[federated.0l7sopl10ed9c510x01et0n646i2].[usr:Calculation_2083625369387018:nk]' />
            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run fontcolor='#757575'>Numofproducts:&#9;</run>
                <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0l7sopl10ed9c510x01et0n646i2].[none:numofproducts:ok]>]]></run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#757575'>Churn Rate:&#9;</run>
                <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0l7sopl10ed9c510x01et0n646i2].[usr:Calculation_2083625272729604:qk]>]]></run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#757575'>Max Churn Flag:&#9;</run>
                <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0l7sopl10ed9c510x01et0n646i2].[usr:Calculation_2083625369387018:nk]>]]></run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true'>Represents how the Churn Rate depends on number of products.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true'>Unsurprisingly 1 product has a higher churn rate than 2 products, but 3 products have a higher churn rate than 1 product and 4 product has a 100% churn rate.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true'>It is so because the people with 3 and 4 products are far too lesser, so when even one of them churns it increases churn rate by a huge percentage.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='pane'>
                <format attr='minwidth' value='741' />
                <format attr='maxwidth' value='741' />
                <format attr='minheight' value='641' />
                <format attr='maxheight' value='641' />
                <format attr='aspect' value='0' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
